<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teispids</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th–6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> · Also known as Teispid dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teispids is the name historians give to the early Persian royal line descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teispes">Teispes</a>, which ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">Anshan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> in the 7th and 6th centuries BCE. Its kings, including Cyrus I and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambyses-i">Cambyses I</a>, used the title king of Anshan, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> came from this family. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> later linked his own Achaemenid line to it, which is why the two are often merged.</p></div>
